### Input configuration
#
# You can get the names of your inputs by running: swaymsg -t get_inputs
# Read `man 5 sway-input` for more information about this section.

# No xkb_layout here on purpose. The layout comes from localectl, which the
# installer writes to /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/00-keyboard.conf, and
# /usr/share/sway/scripts/keyboard.sh applies at startup - see
# $auto_xdg_keyboard in /etc/sway/autostart. A default set here would load
# before that and override the layout the user actually chose.
#
# To pin a layout yourself, set xkb_layout in ~/.config/sway/config.d/;
# keyboard.sh leaves it alone when it finds one. See the shipped
# XX-keyboard.conf.example.
